{"id": "0c517076-01af-458e-947b-907f6e4286ce", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit your EBS setup in us-east-1 in two parts: configuration and data protection (encryption, snapshots, backup policies, volume types), and performance and capacity health from CloudWatch metrics.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_hB3hs9Ba2YspxkbaGgyJuv", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-config-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only production-readiness audit of EBS configuration and data protection in us-east-1. Do NOT make any mutating calls.",
  "context": "User has a production launch next week and wants to know whether their EBS storage is production-ready. Cover every AWS account associated with this agent space (use list_associations to find them; the agent space's host account is 012345678901_1). This slice covers configuration and data protection only; another sub-agent covers performance/CloudWatch metrics.",
  "resources": ["EBS volumes, snapshots, and AMIs in us-east-1", "Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager policies", "AWS Backup plans/vaults covering EBS", "EBS default encryption settings", "EC2 instances the volumes attach to"],
  "timeframe": "current state; snapshot recency over last 30 days",
  "criteria": "Check: (1) unencrypted volumes and whether account-level EBS default encryption is enabled, KMS key type used; (2) volumes without a recent snapshot (>24h/7d) and lack of DLM or AWS Backup coverage; (3) unattached/available volumes and unattached-but-costly leftovers, old snapshots; (4) volume types - gp2 that should be gp3, io1 that should be io2, st1/sc1 used for boot or random IO; (5) DeleteOnTermination on non-root data volumes of production instances; (6) Multi-AZ/single-AZ exposure of stateful workloads, cross-region/cross-account snapshot copy for DR, snapshot lock/recycle bin; (7) volumes in impaired status or with pending modifications; (8) tagging gaps (Name/Environment/Owner). Identify which resources look production (tags/attachments). Give a concise result: counts, a prioritized list of findings (Critical/High/Medium/Low) with specific resource IDs, and suggested fixes. Keep output compact; don't dump raw lists."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit EBS configuration and backups in us-east-1"}, {"id": "tooluse_M5eJwLUPqjiIPQzqUQH6YX", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-perf-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only review of EBS performance and capacity health in us-east-1 using CloudWatch metrics. Do NOT make any mutating calls.",
  "context": "User has a production launch next week and wants to know whether their EBS storage is production-ready and can handle load. Cover every AWS account associated with this agent space (use list_associations; host account is 012345678901_1). This slice covers performance/headroom only; another sub-agent covers configuration, encryption and backups. Start by identifying in-use volumes and attached instances (describe_volumes), focusing on volumes that look production.",
  "resources": ["AWS/EBS CloudWatch metrics for in-use volumes in us-east-1", "EC2 instance-level EBS limits (EBS-optimized, instance EBS bandwidth/IOPS caps) for attached instances"],
  "timeframe": "last 14 days (ending 2026-11-11T19:00:00Z), 5-minute or 1-hour periods as appropriate",
  "criteria": "Check: (1) VolumeQueueLength sustained high, BurstBalance depletion on gp2/st1/sc1, (2) provisioned IOPS/throughput utilization vs. peak (VolumeReadOps+WriteOps, VolumeReadBytes+WriteBytes, VolumeThroughputPercentage/VolumeConsumedReadWriteOps for io1/io2), (3) volumes hitting their limits or the instance-level EBS cap (EBSIOBalance%/EBSByteBalance% for burstable instance types, VolumeIOPSExceeded*/VolumeThroughputExceeded* if available), (4) high latency (VolumeTotalReadTime/WriteTime per op), (5) volumes with little free capacity if CloudWatch agent disk_used_percent is available, (6) CloudWatch alarms existing for EBS-related metrics (describe_alarms) - note missing alarms for critical volumes. Give a compact result: which volumes have little headroom for a launch traffic increase, with volume IDs and numbers, and recommended actions (e.g., gp2->gp3, raise IOPS). Keep output compact."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review EBS performance and headroom metrics in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

